This example is f90_mpif with the mpi module (use mpi) instead of
include "mpif.h".

NOTE: As of SALT-FM v0.6.0, this example works only with the Flang that
SALT-FM is built with. SALT-FM must read the mpi module files, so MPI must
be built with that Flang, and TAU must be configured with that Flang and that
MPI:
$ ./configure -cc=clang -c++=clang++ -fortran=flang -mpi \
    -mpiinc=<mpidir>/include -mpilib=<mpidir>/lib
$ make install

The Makefile sets SALT_BUILD_USES_SALT_FLANG=1, which tells SALT-FM to use
the build's .mod files and MPI's. Without it, saltfm fails with:
error: Cannot parse module file for module 'mpi': Source file 'mpi.saltmod' was not found

To use it:
$ export TAU_MAKEFILE=<taudir>/x86_64/lib/Makefile.tau-clang-mpi
$ ./run.sh

The mpi_f08 module also builds this way, but TAU does not wrap the mpi_f08
MPI_Init, so every rank writes profile.0.0.0.
